With a fingerprint persona whose screen differs from the host's built-in
display (--fingerprint-screen-width and --fingerprint-screen-height, unless
--disable-spoofing contains "screen"), web content on macOS sees the persona's
screen: the built-in display (the primary display when there is none) keeps
its origin but reports the persona's size, and its available area keeps the
real menu bar and Dock insets. Zooming and resizing a browser window on that
display stop at the persona's available area. Without these switches,
behaviour is unchanged.

